# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self Driving Car — what does NOT belong in version control.
#
# Rule of thumb used here: keep anything that is SOURCE or EVIDENCE, drop
# anything a machine regenerates. The bench-test reports and the calibration
# JSON are deliberately KEPT — they are the record of what the hardware
# actually did, and they have already settled one wrong constant.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Model weights & compiled inference engines -----------------------------
# ~25 MB combined, all re-downloadable or rebuildable. The .engine especially:
# TensorRT engines are tied to this exact JetPack/TensorRT version and MUST be
# rebuilt after an upgrade, so committing one would preserve a stale artifact.
*.engine
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth

# --- Kernel module build output (servo/ch341-driver) ------------------------
# The .c source and Makefile are kept; the built module is not.
*.ko
*.o
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.symvers
*.order
.tmp_versions/

# --- SLAM output ------------------------------------------------------------
# room.npy is a 1 MB occupancy grid regenerated by any MAP run. room.png and
# room.meta.json are kept — small, and they document what the map looked like.
# To pin a known-good map anyway:  git add -f "final updates/maps/room.npy"
*.npy

# --- Point clouds (Camera Lab experiments) ---
*.ply

# --- Generated imagery ------------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is written by a script and re-created on the next run.
Camera Lab/scratch_*
Camera Lab/mymap*
Camera Lab/*.log
Camera Control/*.jpg
LiDAR/*.png
robocar/apps/cam_probe/*.jpg
final updates/apps/detect_*.jpg
final updates/apps/fusion_*.jpg
final updates/apps/fusion_*.png
final updates/apps/perception_*.jpg
final updates/apps/selfdrive_*.jpg
final updates/apps/lidar_*.png

# Loose captures at the project root. The photo of the car is ~4.8 MB; if you
# want to keep it:  git add -f 20260625_185831.jpg
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png

# --- Local / transient ---
*.bak
*.log
*.tmp
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store

# --- Recorded sessions (recording/) ---------------------------------------
# Sessions are data, not source: a 10-minute drive is ~10 MB of scans, and a
# session with cameras on is ~1 GB/hour. Keep them out of the repo; archive the
# ones worth keeping somewhere that is not git.
final updates/logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly KEPT, so a future broad pattern doesn't quietly swallow them:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!final updates/apps/*_report.txt          # hardware bench evidence
!final updates/lidar_self_profile.json    # measured self-return mask
!final updates/maps/room.meta.json
!final updates/maps/room.png
!Camera Control/checkerboard_9x6_25mm.pdf # calibration target to print
!robocar/apps/cam_probe/report.txt
!robocar/docs/hardware_report.html
